# Cursor Rules — ClaimSight

## 0. Mandatory references (read BEFORE changing contracts or agents)
- `docs/PROJECT_SPEC.md` — product/agent contracts (§6 is authoritative)
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — system architecture and data flow
- `docs/DECISIONS.md` — locked tradeoffs and deliberate deviations

If a request conflicts with these files, flag it instead of guessing.
Never "fix" behavior that is explicitly recorded in `DECISIONS.md`
back to an older wording of the spec without updating that decision log.

## 1. Scope discipline
- Implement only the slice described in the current task prompt.
- Do not stub later agents (Vision, RAG, Fraud/Risk, Adjudicator), LangGraph,
  Langfuse, or the frontend unless the task asks for them.

## 2. Stack (locked — see PROJECT_SPEC §5)
FastAPI · Celery · Redis · Postgres (+ pgvector later) · SQLAlchemy ·
Hugging Face Transformers · LlamaIndex (RAG slice) · LangGraph (orchestration
slice) · Langfuse (observability slice) · Docker Compose.

Do not substitute without a new entry in `docs/DECISIONS.md`.

## 3. Coding norms
- Concise, senior-engineer fixes; no drive-by refactors outside the task.
- Pydantic models are the agent I/O contracts — keep them aligned with §6 and
  `DECISIONS.md`.
- Prefer honest `None` / empty over hallucinated extractions.
- Tests: default `pytest` must not require Docker or network beyond optional
  `-m hf` model loads.
